{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EkxCx6gsS4z2sZ2X3YcYDW","type":"tool_result","content":"0\tid: srd105-stty\n1\ttitle: \"cmd/stty: Change and Print Terminal Line Settings\"\n2\t\n3\tproblem: |\n4\t  macOS ships a BSD stty that differs from GNU stty in output format and flag naming.\n5\t  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gstty, installed\n6\t  by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by differential testing\n7\t  via pkg/testutils.\n8\t\n9\tgoals:\n10\t  - G1: Print and change terminal line settings.\n11\t  - G2: Support all standard control characters, input/output/local/control mode flags.\n12\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gstty via differential testing.\n13\t\n14\trequirements:\n15\t  R1:\n16\t    title: Default display\n17\t    items:\n18\t      - R1.1:\n19\t          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print a summary of current terminal settings (speed, line discipline, changed-from-default settings) matching GNU stty output format.\n20\t\n21\t  R2:\n22\t    title: All settings display\n23\t    items:\n24\t      - R2.1:\n25\t          text: \"-a or --all must print all current terminal settings in a human-readable format.\"\n26\t\n27\t  R3:\n28\t    title: Save/restore and device\n29\t    items:\n30\t      - R3.1:\n31\t          text: \"-g or --save must print all current terminal settings in a machine-readable format (stty-readable) that can be passed back as arguments to restore settings.\"\n32\t      - R3.2:\n33\t          text: \"-F DEVICE or --file=DEVICE must operate on the specified terminal device instead of stdin.\"\n34\t\n35\t  R4:\n36\t    title: Change settings\n37\t    items:\n38\t      - R4.1:\n39\t          text: \"Must accept setting names as arguments to enable them, and names prefixed with - to disable them (e.g., stty -echo disables echo, stty echo enables it).\"\n40\t\n41\t  R5:\n42\t    title: Special characters\n43\t    items:\n44\t      - R5.1:\n45\t          text: \"Must support special characters: intr, quit, erase, kill, eof, eol, eol2, swtch, start, stop, susp, rprnt, werase, lnext, discard, min, time.\"\n46\t\n47\t  R6:\n48\t    title: Combination and speed settings\n49\t    items:\n50\t      - R6.1:\n51\t          text: \"Must support combination settings: sane (reset to reasonable defaults), cooked (same as -raw), raw (set raw mode), evenp/parity (set even parity), oddp (set odd parity).\"\n52\t      - R6.2:\n53\t          text: \"Must support speed setting: ispeed N, ospeed N, or N alone to set both input and output speed.\"\n54\t\n55\t  R7:\n56\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n57\t    items:\n58\t      - R7.1:\n59\t          text: Must exit 0 on success.\n60\t      - R7.2:\n61\t          text: Must exit 1 on any error (invalid setting, cannot open device).\n62\t      - R7.3:\n63\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n64\t\n65\tnon_goals:\n66\t  - cmd/stty does not implement all obscure termios flags; it covers the commonly used set matching GNU stty output.\n67\t\n68\tacceptance_criteria:\n69\t  - id: AC1\n70\t    criterion: \"stty with no arguments prints terminal settings summary, matching gstty.\"\n71\t    traces:\n72\t      - R1.1\n73\t  - id: AC2\n74\t    criterion: \"stty -a prints all settings, matching gstty -a.\"\n75\t    traces:\n76\t      - R2.1\n77\t  - id: AC3\n78\t    criterion: \"stty -g prints machine-readable settings, matching gstty -g.\"\n79\t    traces:\n80\t      - R3.1\n81\t  - id: AC4\n82\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gstty passes.\"\n83\t    traces:\n84\t      - R1.1\n85\t      - R2.1\n86\t      - R3.1\n87\t  - id: AC5\n88\t    criterion: \"cmd/stty compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n89\t    traces:\n90\t      - R1.1\n91\t      - R2.1\n92\t      - R3.1\n93\t      - R3.2\n94\t      - R4.1\n95\t      - R5.1\n96\t      - R6.1\n97\t      - R6.2\n98\t      - R7.1\n99\t      - R7.2\n100\t      - R7.3\n101\t\n102\tpackage_contract:\n103\t  imports:\n104\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n105\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f584f668-1d5b-4e5a-b50f-af9f46c250c3","uuid":"e3f30fdf-2b0e-427c-a502-9b6ad5ce56f3","timestamp":"2026-05-29T17:18:14.975Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5656/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd105-stty.yaml","content":"id: srd105-stty\ntitle: \"cmd/stty: Change and Print Terminal Line Settings\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships a BSD stty that differs from GNU stty in output format and flag naming.\n  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gstty, installed\n  by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by differential testing\n  via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print and change terminal line settings.\n  - G2: Support all standard control characters, input/output/local/control mode flags.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gstty via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default display\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print a summary of current terminal settings (speed, line discipline, changed-from-default settings) matching GNU stty output format.\n\n  R2:\n    title: All settings display\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-a or --all must print all current terminal settings in a human-readable format.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Save/restore and device\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-g or --save must print all current terminal settings in a machine-readable format (stty-readable) that can be passed back as arguments to restore settings.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"-F DEVICE or --file=DEVICE must operate on the specified terminal device instead of stdin.\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Change settings\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: \"Must accept setting names as arguments to enable them, and names prefixed with - to disable them (e.g., stty -echo disables echo, stty echo enables it).\"\n\n  R5:\n    title: Special characters\n    items:\n      - R5.1:\n          text: \"Must support special characters: intr, quit, erase, kill, eof, eol, eol2, swtch, start, stop, susp, rprnt, werase, lnext, discard, min, time.\"\n\n  R6:\n    title: Combination and speed settings\n    items:\n      - R6.1:\n          text: \"Must support combination settings: sane (reset to reasonable defaults), cooked (same as -raw), raw (set raw mode), evenp/parity (set even parity), oddp (set odd parity).\"\n      - R6.2:\n          text: \"Must support speed setting: ispeed N, ospeed N, or N alone to set both input and output speed.\"\n\n  R7:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R7.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 on success.\n      - R7.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 on any error (invalid setting, cannot open device).\n      - R7.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/stty does not implement all obscure termios flags; it covers the commonly used set matching GNU stty output.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"stty with no arguments prints terminal settings summary, matching gstty.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"stty -a prints all settings, matching gstty -a.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"stty -g prints machine-readable settings, matching gstty -g.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gstty passes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R3.1\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/stty compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R4.1\n      - R5.1\n      - R6.1\n      - R6.2\n      - R7.1\n      - R7.2\n      - R7.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":106,"startLine":0,"totalLines":106}}}
